WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:09.540
Paris Habitat needs a GIS platform. Radar's verdict for our Lyon web agency: a weak fit. Mapping isn't what it does.

2
00:00:10.491 --> 00:00:16.751
But in France, small firms can bid together as a groupement, and TED records every one.

3
00:00:18.891 --> 00:00:23.291
Radar finds the tenders you can win, and the partners to win them with.

4
00:00:24.647 --> 00:00:31.807
It reads the notice against your profile, and pinpoints the gaps: GIS, and application maintenance.

5
00:00:34.862 --> 00:00:40.682
Then it ranks partners who cover them, with their TED awards and past joint bids as evidence.

6
00:00:43.902 --> 00:00:48.182
It drafts the invitation in French. You send it from your own mailbox.

7
00:00:51.462 --> 00:00:58.842
Replies are scored, references are checked against TED, and every partner who answers can open a radar of their own.

8
00:01:01.333 --> 00:01:03.433
Every claim comes with a receipt.

9
00:01:05.263 --> 00:01:07.863
Stop bidding alone. Try the live demo.

